Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 10:03:24 +1000
Subject: [PATCH 16/38] Shaders: one back edge per loop header

vkd3d-proton's DXIL conversion keeps one back edge per loop header, as
DXC's code has. With several, the others stay in the header's forward
predecessors and form a cycle, and in programs with wave shuffles its
dominator search then recursed without end: the thread overflowed its
stack and, under Wine, hung. The ray-tracing shadow passes do this once
they translate. The back edges of a header with several now go through
one new block that joins their phi values.

(cherry picked from commit d48ec767ba89d27090f6f61d3a9ebfd9f5374def)
(cherry picked from commit 364c1bc45c4510d0d07a1e58efaff8644165ded2)
